            <ArticleTitle>Factitious pain and swelling of the upper arm. Case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>71-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>After a trivial injury, a 16-year-old girl had pain, disability and oedema in her right arm. In a first operation the suspectedly entrapped ulnar nerve was anteposed, and in a second--because symptoms worsened--it was retroposed. The condition proved to be self-induced, by compression of the arm with a bandage.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
